---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MiniCalc from "../components/MiniCalc.tsx";
---
<Layout title="BMR calculator — MacroChat">
  <section class="section calc-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div style="max-width:46rem; margin-bottom:2rem;">
        <span class="pill">Free tools · No signup</span>
        <h1 style="margin:1rem 0 0.8rem;">BMR calculator</h1>
        <p class="hero__lead" style="margin:0;">
          Basal Metabolic Rate — the calories your body burns at complete rest just
          keeping you alive. It's the floor your daily calorie target is built on.
        </p>
      </div>
      <MiniCalc mode="bmr" client:load />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section calc-doc" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:52rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 style="margin:0.6rem 0 1rem;">Mifflin-St Jeor</h2>
      <pre><code>BMR = 10 · weight(kg) + 6.25 · height(cm) − 5 · age + s
  s = +5 (male)   s = −161 (female)</code></pre>
      <p>Enter a body-fat % and it switches to <b>Katch-McArdle</b>
        (<code>370 + 21.6 · lean mass</code>), which is more accurate for lean or
        very heavy people.</p>
      <p>Multiply BMR by an activity factor to get your
        <a href="/tdee-calculator">TDEE</a>, or use the
        <a href="/calculator">full calculator</a> for a goal-adjusted target.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
